  "exportLabel": "Molen original complete Belvedere palaces exterior shared surfaces source",
  "expectedDraftMasterHash": "sha256:c500e0a9ec0070faf0ea23bf14bd6c25701955e206130ad631d7bcd0b8193424",
  "visualBrief": "Both individual principal Belvedere palaces: the complete Upper palace with three raised mansard-roofed central blocks and four domed corner pavilions, and the complete Lower palace with raised central hall, red hipped/mansard roofs and its actual bent rear courtyard ranges. Gardens, ponds, detached annexes and city buildings remain native context. Original exterior geometry; no interiors or copied sculpture.",
  "heightPolicy": "Picture-guided relative palace heights on an approximate182m standard Terrarium reference. Upper threshold194m (pool front195.7m), Lower threshold173.3m. Separate occupied foundations and bounded entry transitions meet the unchanged coarse field; no garden flattening. Lower native central height28m is inconsistent with its photographed one-story frontage/raised hall and is not treated as a surveyed dimension. Historic thresholds and roof heights remain approximate.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X ENE along theUpper palace; -X WSW; +Z SSE toward theUpper reflecting pool; -Z NNW toward theLower palace/gardens. +Y up.",
