    "terrainTiles": 2,
    "heightBasis": "Picture-guided relative palace heights on an approximate182m standard Terrarium reference. Upper threshold194m (pool front195.7m), Lower threshold173.3m. Separate occupied foundations and bounded entry transitions meet the unchanged coarse field; no garden flattening. Lower native central height28m is inconsistent with its photographed one-story frontage/raised hall and is not treated as a surveyed dimension. Historic thresholds and roof heights remain approximate."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Both individual principal Belvedere palaces: the complete Upper palace with three raised mansard-roofed central blocks and four domed corner pavilions, and the complete Lower palace with raised central hall, red hipped/mansard roofs and its actual bent rear courtyard ranges. Gardens, ponds, detached annexes and city buildings remain native context. Original exterior geometry; no interiors or copied sculpture.",
    "Picture-guided relative palace heights on an approximate182m standard Terrarium reference. Upper threshold194m (pool front195.7m), Lower threshold173.3m. Separate occupied foundations and bounded entry transitions meet the unchanged coarse field; no garden flattening. Lower native central height28m is inconsistent with its photographed one-story frontage/raised hall and is not treated as a surveyed dimension. Historic thresholds and roof heights remain approximate.",
    "Fine ornaments, window inventories, concealed roof joins and historic grade are original approximations. No copied statues, heraldry or inscriptions. The coarse global elevation field is not surveyed; bounded thresholds approximate contact, not historic stairs. Physical-device timings and numerical LOD errors remain unmeasured.",
    "Seven existing256px plaster,limestone,granite,painted metal,ceramic tile,window grid andpainted wood graphs. Original metric UVs andlinear colors; no private or embedded images. Skyline retains both principal silhouettes, openLower forecourt, four Upper domes andthree raised crowns; district adds sparse recessed glazing; street adds frames; close-up adds dormers,pilasters,balustrades andoriginal ornaments. Source preserves finer profiles. Numerical LOD errors3/1.5/.7/.25m andphysical timings are unmeasured."
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "url": "https://jooinn.com/vienna-belvedere.html",
      "observed": "Upper-palace aerial actually inspected: four green domed corner pavilions, three raised central green mansard/hipped blocks, long lower wings and terraced garden-facing frontage, projecting pool-side entry. This picture shows the Upper palace, not the whole two-palace campus. Independent annexes and city blocks remain map context."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belweder_g%C3%B3rny.jpg",
      "observed": "Pool-side Upper frontage actually inspected: three tall arched central closed entries below a curved white crown, tall rectangular glazing, white/cream pilasters and cornices, three distinct green central roof crowns, green domed corner pavilions, dormers/chimneys and original simplified urn rhythm. No copied sculpture, heraldry or text."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://connectingvienna.com/vienna/museums/lower-belvedere/",
      "observed": "Lower garden front actually inspected: long white single principal story, red hipped/mansard roofs with small dormers/chimneys, raised central three-window hall, white pierced balustrades and simplified original urns, green closed central/side doors and tall rectangular glazing. PMTiles supplies its bent rear courtyard ranges, which are included; independent western annexes remain native."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/5887599",
      "observed": "Standard Protomaps PMTiles direct signed frame: Upper way5887599 andLower way31313338, all four parent fragments andall attached overlapping part fragments, grouped by native identity. Independent western annexes3/7 andurban context retained."
    }
